      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_1971668492": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-1f15d09fdf@example.invalid",
          "leftPadding": "3",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-b3eaac8b1c@example.invalid",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Feb 06 2025 18:52:38 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><b>Proven. </b></span></span><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><b><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Adaptable. Comprehensive.</span></span></b></span></h2>\n<p>MEDPOR has been a trusted name in the industry since 1985, with hundreds of thousands of procedures performed, and hundreds of published clinical reports in reconstructive, cranial, oculoplastic, and&nbsp;cosmetic applications.</p>\n<p>Our MEDPOR product line provides you an array of porous polyethylene solutions for your reconstruction and augmentation needs. We understand that bio-compatibility characteristics of implants are paramount to help surgeons achieve positive patient outcomes. The omni-directional pore structure of our polyethylene implants may increase implant acceptance by allowing the patient‘s native tissue to integrate with the implant. In addition to our comprehensive line of stock MEDPOR implants, we offer CT-based&nbsp;patient-specific implants, putting the implant design in your hands.<br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Feb 28 2025 22:23:28 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "rightPadding": "5",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
